(4931339, 715842, 20577, '<td valign="top">Did you know that faulty records enable terrorists, illegal aliens and criminals to purchase guns? Over a two and a half-year period, at least 9,976 convicted felons and other illegal buyers in 46 states obtained guns because of inadequate records. Are you an illegal alien who got your guns because of faulty records? You kind of look like an illegal alien in this picture. I would guess you are from Mars or something because you have a really big head and your eyes look like they are closer than a normal human. Don''t think for a minute that there aren''t aliens from Mars roaming around this planet with illegal guns. Aliens are smart and they know how to trick people into making faulty records so they can get guns to shoot people with. I remember this one time I was minding my own business at a bank and out of the blue some crazy guy pulls out a gun and tells everyone to "GET ON THE FLOOR". While I was lying on the floor in a puddle of my own pee I got the courage to ask him if he had obtained the guns legally and OF COURSE he didn''t. He said he got them because of faulty records. I gave him a really dirty look to show him I was disappointed in America for their faulty record keeping. He just laughed at me and said... "Zulak beba hono gazo luka" which translates to "America has faulty gun record keeping and I laugh at you with my illegal guns in my hand you smelly human" I know Martian, so I was able to translate... Anyway, I think a tighter crop would have been better. Also, your title leads me to believe that you are indeed from Mars because Elmer Fudd was from Mars and you two both have the same head shape. Wait... is this Elmer Fudd? If so... "Hano lioka betuka jangy freida bigo pigga"</td>', 'Did you know that faulty records enable terrorists, illegal aliens and criminals to purchase guns? Over a two and a half-year period, at least 9,976 convicted felons and other illegal buyers in 46 states obtained guns because of inadequate records. Are you an illegal alien who got your guns because of faulty records? You kind of look like an illegal alien in this picture. I would guess you are from Mars or something because you have a really big head and your eyes look like they are closer than a normal human. Don''t think for a minute that there aren''t aliens from Mars roaming around this planet with illegal guns. Aliens are smart and they know how to trick people into making faulty records so they can get guns to shoot people with. I remember this one time I was minding my own business at a bank and out of the blue some crazy guy pulls out a gun and tells everyone to "GET ON THE FLOOR". While I was lying on the floor in a puddle of my own pee I got the courage to ask him if he had obtained the guns legally and OF COURSE he didn''t. He said he got them because of faulty records. I gave him a really dirty look to show him I was disappointed in America for their faulty record keeping. He just laughed at me and said... "Zulak beba hono gazo luka" which translates to "America has faulty gun record keeping and I laugh at you with my illegal guns in my hand you smelly human" I know Martian, so I was able to translate... Anyway, I think a tighter crop would have been better. Also, your title leads me to believe that you are indeed from Mars because Elmer Fudd was from Mars and you two both have the same head shape. Wait... is this Elmer Fudd? If so... "Hano lioka betuka jangy freida bigo pigga"', '2008-09-03 13:57:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(4931561, 716500, 65234, '<td valign="top">Can us shelter volunteers have some, too?  That would come in REALLY handy come next summer.  In fact, when the challenge is over I need to remember to forward this to my friends at the shelter.  The image may end up with its own fan club!<br/> <br/>Major bonus point for such a creative subject, even if you only were clever enough to see the opportunity :-)</td>', 'Can us shelter volunteers have some, too?  That would come in REALLY handy come next summer.  In fact, when the challenge is over I need to remember to forward this to my friends at the shelter.  The image may end up with its own fan club! Major bonus point for such a creative subject, even if you only were clever enough to see the opportunity :-)', '2008-09-03 15:03:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(4931595, 715809, 65234, '<td valign="top">Egads; that''s my alma mater with the National Cathedral in the background!  Everything looks much closer together than it appears in real life ... interesting perspective.  Now I''m trying to figure out where you took it from and with what length lens ;-)<br/> <br/>Back to the challenge:  two big towers each on old buildings, and I''ll ignore all the dissimilarities.  Very nice detail on the buildings, especially considering how far apart they really are.</td>', 'Egads; that''s my alma mater with the National Cathedral in the background!  Everything looks much closer together than it appears in real life ... interesting perspective.  Now I''m trying to figure out where you took it from and with what length lens ;-) Back to the challenge:  two big towers each on old buildings, and I''ll ignore all the dissimilarities.  Very nice detail on the buildings, especially considering how far apart they really are.', '2008-09-03 15:14:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(4931603, 715842, 65234, '<td valign="top">Good thing none of mine are named Bugs!  Fun ... er, shot.</td>', 'Good thing none of mine are named Bugs!  Fun ... er, shot.', '2008-09-03 15:15:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(4931635, 716414, 65234, '<td valign="top">I''m a little confused by the spotting and outlines on the birds and below them in a few places on the tree.  It doesn''t match the rest of the image in terms of realism which is disconcerting to me.</td>', 'I''m a little confused by the spotting and outlines on the birds and below them in a few places on the tree.  It doesn''t match the rest of the image in terms of realism which is disconcerting to me.', '2008-09-03 15:27:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(4931638, 717001, 65234, '<td valign="top">I love this :-)  Great take (so to speak) on the challenge and a heartwarming image.</td>', 'I love this :-)  Great take (so to speak) on the challenge and a heartwarming image.', '2008-09-03 15:28:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(4931647, 716656, 65234, '<td valign="top">Those''re slugs.  Slugs are evil and make holes in my garden.  I will try to overlook my dislike of them ;-)<br/> <br/>Your fungus is well lit and your composition is good; maybe could use a little more light on the evil ones.  And if you could have caught both of them with "horns" extended that would have been even better.</td>', 'Those''re slugs.  Slugs are evil and make holes in my garden.  I will try to overlook my dislike of them ;-) Your fungus is well lit and your composition is good; maybe could use a little more light on the evil ones.  And if you could have caught both of them with "horns" extended that would have been even better.', '2008-09-03 15:32:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(4931652, 716620, 65234, '<td valign="top">No, no; don''t jump, ladies!!!  Oh, wait; that looks more like a bench than a ledge.  Never mind ;-)</td>', 'No, no; don''t jump, ladies!!!  Oh, wait; that looks more like a bench than a ledge.  Never mind ;-)', '2008-09-03 15:36:12.000000', NULL, 1),
