(4944664, 716338, 50034, '<td valign="top">Congratulations, Lady!  The other comments, your placement, and score have already identified you skills and this photos as par excellence!  :)<br/> <br/>The Best I can hope to do is give a hearty AMEN!  I pray that one day my skills will excel as yours have...<br/> <br/>The only thought that I would like to add is a compliment to your subjects.  They truly are so identical that I would be willing to guess that they can finish each other''s sentences.  They probably could substitute on dates for each other due to last minute scheduling issues (without a boyfriend catching on too quickly.)<br/> <br/>Finally, I think sometimes it''s fun to take a "wild guess" about something based on scientific probability just to see how close you come.  <br/> <br/>Therefore, based on what I know of muscles and the way they are used and defined through repetition, I would guess that the girl on the left is on-average more serious than the girl on the right because her slight smile looks more deliberate and less defined.  The girl on the right has extra dimples with the one on the corner of the mouth being more defined,...all of which indicates an easier and more natural smile made effortlessly.<br/> <br/>Maybe this knowledge is worth something to somebody, but it is just another indication of how I look at life...in the macro.  <br/> <br/>Thank You for enduring my impromptu critique...Bottom Line: This is a Great Portrait and the Black &amp; White really sells it!  :)</td>', 'Congratulations, Lady!  The other comments, your placement, and score have already identified you skills and this photos as par excellence!  :) The Best I can hope to do is give a hearty AMEN!  I pray that one day my skills will excel as yours have... The only thought that I would like to add is a compliment to your subjects.  They truly are so identical that I would be willing to guess that they can finish each other''s sentences.  They probably could substitute on dates for each other due to last minute scheduling issues (without a boyfriend catching on too quickly.) Finally, I think sometimes it''s fun to take a "wild guess" about something based on scientific probability just to see how close you come.   Therefore, based on what I know of muscles and the way they are used and defined through repetition, I would guess that the girl on the left is on-average more serious than the girl on the right because her slight smile looks more deliberate and less defined.  The girl on the right has extra dimples with the one on the corner of the mouth being more defined,...all of which indicates an easier and more natural smile made effortlessly. Maybe this knowledge is worth something to somebody, but it is just another indication of how I look at life...in the macro.   Thank You for enduring my impromptu critique...Bottom Line: This is a Great Portrait and the Black & White really sells it!  :)', '2008-09-09 15:46:10.000000', NULL, 0),
